# Stickman Idle — Core Rules

Godot 4.7 idle RPG with transparent desktop overlay. Prioritize repository context over generic training knowledge.

## Required reading (in order)

1. `AGENTS.md`
2. `docs/KNOWLEDGE_GRAPH.md`
3. `docs/architecture/overview.md`
4. Domain doc for your edit area (`combat.md`, `inventory.md`, etc.)
5. `docs/architecture/save-format.md` if touching persistence

## Target module layout

| Module | Responsibility |
|--------|----------------|
| `domains/combat/` | Combat loop, party, drops, skill runtime |
| `domains/inventory/` | Inventory, equip, forge, warehouse rules |
| `domains/progression/` | XP, worlds, skill tree, StatCalculator |
| `presentation/` | HUD, menus, `tr()`, window manager |
| `core/` | GameState, SaveService, wiring |
| `data/` | Resources and schemas |
| `platform/` | Autoloads (audio, item database) |

All code uses English folder and file names (`scenes/`, `domains/`, `data/skills/`, `presentation/`, `platform/`).

## Module boundaries

- Domain code must NOT reference UI nodes.
- Presentation must NOT implement economy or combat rules.
- Progression must NOT mutate gold directly — go through GameState/signals.
- `core/` wires services; avoid feature god-objects.

## Language

- Code: English (functions, signals, files, classes)
- Player-facing UI: `tr("KEY")` + `locales/*.po`
- Docs: English

## Save changes

- `SAVE_VERSION` lives in save service (`SAVE_VERSION = 4` today in `core/save_service.gd`)
- Bump version + migration + update `docs/architecture/save-format.md`

## Minimum playtest after combat/inventory/save changes

See `docs/workflows/playtest-checklist.md`
